<title>SINGAPORE: First Capital Corp 1996 net up 62 pct.</title>
<headline>First Capital Corp 1996 net up 62 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Dec 31 1996</p>
<p>( in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 92.67   vs    57.35</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	   34.60   vs    23.20</p>
<p>    Group share (fully diluted)  34.10   vs    19.20</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		    5.0    vs     nil</p>
<p>Turnover			  371.98   vs   224.85</p>
<p>    Investment income		 5.09   vs     7.12</p>
<p>    Other/interest income	   7.72   vs     2.41</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  7.72   vs     7.86</p>
<p>    Operating pretax profit     143.21   vs    98.80</p>
<p>Income from associates	  2.23   vs     3.58 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				  39.92   vs    29.72</p>
<p>    Minorities	   (loss)    12.86   vs     8.15  (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   nil    vs    32.26</p>
<p>Note - Property-based First Capital Corp said development activities at five plots of land in Singapore would start in 1997 and 1998.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
